I have everything needed. Here is the complete report on the owner-creation REST endpoint.

## Summary of findings

The DTOs are **not** named `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse`. They are generated by OpenAPI codegen from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: the request body is `OwnerFieldsDto` (schema `OwnerFields`) and the response is `OwnerDto` (schema `Owner`). There are no hand-written `OwnerFieldsDto.java`/`OwnerDto.java` sources in the tree (they are generated at build time), so I've included the OpenAPI schemas that define them.

---

## 1. Endpoint YAML

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: normalizeTelephone

normalizeTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: normalizeEmail

normalizeEmail:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.NormalizeOwnerEmail
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: rejectDuplicateTelephone

rejectDuplicateTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: assignCustomerCode

assignCustomerCode:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AssignOwnerCustomerCode
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

The chain is: `BuildOwner` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` → `NormalizeOwnerEmail` → `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone` → `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` → `SaveOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerCreated`. All run under the `transaction` governance.

---

## 2. Referenced Java function classes

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

import net.officefloor.plugin.variable.Out;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper.OwnerMapper;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerFieldsDto;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;

public class BuildOwner {

    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
        require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
        require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
        require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
        require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
        require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
            throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        }
        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
        }
        built.set(owner);
    }

    private static void require(String field, String value, List<String> missing) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
            missing.add(field);
        }
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`

