## 3. Owner entity, request/response DTOs, and mapper

### Owner entity
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — extends `Person` (which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`). Fields: `address` (`@NotEmpty`), `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `telephone` (`@NotEmpty`, `@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$` E.164), `email`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`), and `pets` (`Set<Pet>`, eager, cascade all). Standard getters/setters for each; `lastName`/`firstName` come from the `Person` superclass (see `getLastName()` used in `toString()` and the mapper). Notably there is **no** `address` structured breakdown — a single flat `String address` column.

Relevant field declarations:
```java
@Column(name = "address")
@NotEmpty
private String address;

@Column(name = "city")
@NotEmpty
private String city;

@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be E.164, e.g. +61412345678")
private String telephone;
