Note the request `telephone` pattern is digits-only (`^[0-9]*$`) — the E.164 `+` form is produced server-side by `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`. `address` is a single flat string; there are no `addressLine1`/`postcode`/`sharesHousehold` fields in the current schema (the acceptance test references those as not-yet-implemented — see section 6).

