(The duplicate-telephone handler references a `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper in the same `escalation` package.) There are also generic escalation handlers in that folder — `java.lang.Exception.yml`, `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml`, `...MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml`, `...NotFoundException.yml`, `...AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` — if you need those too.

---

## 6. Tests related to creating owners

There is one owner-creation acceptance test plus its base class. Both use black-box `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.status;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** household-duplicate: Reject creating an owner when another owner has the same lastName and the same address (co... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText()); b.put("address", a.get("address").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}

	@Test
	void functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
		b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText()); b.put("address", a.get("address").asText());
		b.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		createOwner(b).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
	}
}
```

Important observations about this test (it describes a **not-yet-implemented "household-duplicate" rule**):
- `coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress` expects a **409 Conflict** when a second owner has the same `lastName` **and** `address` as an existing owner. The current pipeline only rejects duplicate **telephone** (via `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone`); there is no last-name+address check, so this test would currently fail.
- `functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress` expects that same `lastName` but different `address` is allowed (2xx).
- `functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold` expects that a new request-body field `sharesHousehold: true` overrides the duplicate rejection. That field does **not** exist in the `OwnerFields` OpenAPI schema yet, and `BuildOwner`/mapper do not read it.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the base harness (full contents were read). Key helpers your implementation must satisfy:
- `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`.
- `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner: `firstName="Test"`, unique `lastName` (`"Sur"+letters`), unique `address` (`"<n> Test Street"`), unique `city` (`"Town<n>"`), unique `telephone` (`"04%08d"`, a 10-digit AU mobile).
- `createOwner(body)` → `POST /api/owners`; `createOwnerOk(body)` asserts 2xx and returns the new id via `extractId` (reads `id` from body, else parses the `Location` header).
- `getOwner(id)` / `fetchOwner(id)` → `GET /api/owners/{id}`.
- There are also helpers hinting at broader rule sets not yet in the schema: `withPostcode` (`postcode`), `structuredOwner` (`addressLine1`+`postcode`, removes flat `address`), `createOwnerWithKey` (`Idempotency-Key` header), `deleteOwner` (soft-delete via `DELETE /api/owners/{id}`), plus pinned reference tables (`CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `HOLIDAYS`) and `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` helpers.

The two other files in that package are supporting infrastructure, not owner-creation tests themselves: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`.

Note: no unit tests exist for the individual owner functions (no `*Test.java` under `function/owner`); the only owner-creation coverage is the acceptance test above.

